  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding from Alaska Medicaid Bimzelx (bimekizumab-bkzx), an IL-17A and F antagonist. Version 2; Original: 07/15/2024; Accepted: 9/20/2024; Effective: 11/1/2024; Updated: 11/21/2025.",
    "Closed indication labels attest to FDA diagnosis, severity and systemic therapy or phototherapy candidacy where applicable. All five indications require age \u226518.",
    "PsO/PsA alone require current weight and baseline liver enzymes, alkaline phosphatase and bilirubin. CASPAR submission is encoded in the PsA severity fact. Baseline PASI submission requires manual review on the PsO BSA and concomitant severe PsA paths; those selections do not independently establish PASI submission.",
    "PsA conventional-agent option includes documented clinical contraindication as requested by the encoding specification; the PDF approval #4 explicitly states trial and failure, without a contraindication exception. Manually review contraindication-only PsA conventional-agent attestations.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization approval up to 12 months.",
    "Quantity limits (manual review): PSO 320mg/28d; PsA/nr-axSpA/AS 160mg/28d; HS induction 320mg every 2 weeks at Weeks 0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, then maintenance 320mg/28d.",
    "Cautions (notes only): risk of suicidal ideation and behavior; avoid active tuberculosis (TB) and treat latent TB before treatment; monitor LFTs, alkaline phosphatase and bilirubin; live vaccines are not recommended.",
    "PDL status unknown: this criteria PDF is silent. Alternatives require indication-specific review and do not imply coverage.",
    "Remaining gaps: baseline PASI documentation on non-PASI PsO paths, source discrepancy for PsA conventional-agent contraindications, duration, reauthorization, dosing, quantity enforcement and cautions require manual review."
  ],
